rts at 2..5? i=2..5 with Pia left.\\\\n\\\\nClue 5: E between Y and W. E at i+1. So Y and W on opposite sides of E: one left, one right. Clue 2: L between W and Y. Since W/Y opposite sides of E, L somewhere between them. Need consider.\\\\n\\\\nClue 1: Y next to C. C at i. Y adjacent to C. Cneighbors are i-1 and i+1. i+1 is E, so Y must be at i-1. But Pia is also left of C, not necessarily at i-1. Wait if Y at i-1, then Pia cannot be there but can be further left. But clue 5 E between Y and W: Y at i-1 left of E, so W must be right of E (position > i+1). Good. But if Y at i-1, then C's left neighbor is Y, and E's left neighbor C, triple Y-C-E-A consecutive. Also Pia left of C, so i>=3? Because need position left of C for Pia, and Y occupies i-1. If i=2, Y at1, no seat left for Pia. So i>=3. Triple positions Y,C,E,A = i-1,i,i+1,i+2. Pia somewhere < i-1? Actually C between Pia and E: C at i, E at i+1, Pia < i. But seat i-1 occupied Y, so Pia < i-1. Thus i>=3.\\\\n\\\\nThen W right of E (>i+2? A at i+2, so W > i+1, could be i+2? no occupied A, so >i+2). Liam between W and Y. Y at i-1, W > i+2. So L position must be > i-1 and < W. Available positions maybe between C/E/A? occupied. Since consecutive block Y C E A occupies i-1 to i+2. There is no available between Y and A except occupied. Liam cannot be in occupied. Since W is to right of A, for L to be between Y and W, L could be at positions i...? But all between Y and W that are < W include C,E,A occupied and maybe seats between A and W if W not immediately after A. If W = i+3, then no seat between A and W; L cannot. If W > i+3, L can be between A and W. So possible with gap after A. Need seats.\\\\n\\\\nTotal 7. Block length 4 from i-1 to i+2. Pia left of block. W and Liam right of block maybe. i can be 3,4,5? Need Pia left of Y (p < i\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483394,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":190,\\\"total_